#NEXUS

[ mcdonald2011a_fig1: Rectangular strict consensus with many polytomies (as listed below). Where a node's stem meets its vertical at the height of one of its branches (Iguanacolossus, Tethyshadros) the branch is read as leaving that node. Node numbers 1-9 are not clade names and are not encoded; the yellow and blue highlights behind Camptosaurus, Cumnoria and Uteodon are not part of the tree. 46 tips, 9 polytomies (3, 6, 3, 5, 4, 4, 3, 4, 5 children). Sample 10 case (census 3, seed 20261274). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

